WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.175 --> 00:00:01.949
(snowmobile engine)

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:04.338
(light music)

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:05.531
- [Voiceover] A lot of people call this

00:00:05.531 --> 00:00:07.022
the Dr. Seuss house.

00:00:07.022 --> 00:00:08.595
- First of all, nobody asked Dr. Seuss

00:00:08.595 --> 00:00:10.762
for permission to do that.

00:00:12.014 --> 00:00:13.634
They refer to that because of some

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:16.551
of the ideas that Dr. Seuss had.

00:00:17.697 --> 00:00:18.844
I think he was a genius,

00:00:18.844 --> 00:00:21.597
and I think he did a lot
of good for the world.

00:00:21.597 --> 00:00:23.386
I try and write poetry,

00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:27.469
and I kind of think of
this as a poem to the sky.

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:33.944
I am Phillip Paul Weidner,

00:00:33.944 --> 00:00:36.289
I'm the owner and builder
of Goose Creek Tower.

00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:38.899
I went to MIT, and I'm kind
of a frustrated architect,

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:42.068
so I like building. I just
designed it out of my head,

00:00:42.068 --> 00:00:45.021
we didn't have blueprints,
we drew it out on cardboard,

00:00:45.021 --> 00:00:47.399
plywood, just as we were going.

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:48.569
What I'm going to end
up doing, eventually,

00:00:48.569 --> 00:00:50.947
is put some hooks here and
hang pots and pans off them,

00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:52.305
because this is the kitchen.

00:00:52.305 --> 00:00:56.349
I started to build a 
40-by-40 ascribed log cabin,

00:00:56.349 --> 00:00:58.090
and I realized I could put pillars on top,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.685
and put another house on top a house.

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:01.716
And I just kept going,

00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:04.110
we got to 185 feet and we stopped,

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.909
because 200 feet is federal air space.

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:10.101
Now I just have to finish it out.

00:01:10.101 --> 00:01:13.051
This is pretty much the last real stairs.

00:01:13.051 --> 00:01:14.377
There are multiple levels in there,

00:01:14.377 --> 00:01:16.825
and I've tried to count them,
and it's just impossible.

00:01:16.825 --> 00:01:19.000
It depends on how you count stories.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.912
(light music)

00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:23.387
I wanted to be able to see,

00:01:23.387 --> 00:01:24.824
and that's the reason I went up.

00:01:24.824 --> 00:01:28.384
You can actually see
for at least 300 miles,

00:01:28.384 --> 00:01:31.980
and of course, when the
Northern Lights are out,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.780
you can really see.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.116
(light music)

00:01:36.116 --> 00:01:40.318
I hope that Goose Creek Tower
will inspire other people,

00:01:40.318 --> 00:01:43.376
to do worthwhile things,
not just in building,

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:45.376
but whatever they do with their life.

00:01:45.376 --> 00:01:49.490
And every time I go up there
it's a different experience.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.458
It kind of gives you a sense of the

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:53.484
enormity of the universe.

00:01:53.484 --> 00:01:56.067
(light music)

